Files
-----
Every file below carries the declaration in its own header, naming its
upstream source and the date it was taken. This list is the index to those
headers, not a replacement for them.

Copied whole — 18 files, all 2026-09-07. Header declaration only.

  crates/adapters/src/config.rs
  crates/adapters/src/error.rs
  crates/adapters/src/model_capabilities.rs
  crates/adapters/src/provider.rs
  crates/adapters/src/claude_desktop_config.rs
  crates/adapters/src/gemini_config.rs
  crates/adapters/src/grok_config.rs
  crates/adapters/src/opencode_config.rs
  crates/adapters/src/gateway_takeover.rs
  crates/adapters/src/proxy/error.rs
  crates/adapters/src/proxy/error_mapper.rs
  crates/adapters/src/proxy/json_canonical.rs
  crates/adapters/src/proxy/model_mapper.rs
  crates/adapters/src/proxy/sse.rs
  crates/adapters/src/proxy/tool_media.rs
  crates/adapters/src/proxy/providers/streaming.rs
  crates/adapters/src/proxy/providers/transform.rs
  crates/gateway/src/strategy/circuit_breaker.rs

  Two of these are not a one-to-one rename. `gateway_takeover.rs` folds four
  upstream files — `src-tauri/src/{opencode,openclaw,hermes,pi}_config.rs` —
  into one, and `crates/gateway/src/strategy/circuit_breaker.rs` comes from
  `src-tauri/src/proxy/circuit_breaker.rs`, which lives outside the `proxy`
  tree the rest were taken from. Both say so in their own headers.

Ported function by function — 1 file. Header declaration plus a
`// Ported from cc-switch: <upstream path>::<function>` annotation above
each ported function, so any one of them can be diffed against its origin.

  crates/adapters/src/codex_config.rs
      Copied on 2026-09-07 as the config write core. The gates and repairs
      around that writer — the ones that decide whether a configuration
      Codex would refuse to load ever reaches disk — were ported on
      2026-09-11; the file's header lists both. The ~6k lines of
      managed-OAuth logic remain deliberately unported, because Kiwano
      hosts no OAuth: there is no CLI-rotated token to preserve, which is
      what that logic exists to protect.

Upstream of both crates is the same project and the same licence, so the
notice above covers all 19 files. Nothing outside `crates/adapters` and
`crates/gateway` is derived from cc-switch — the app, the gateway server,
the routing and the UI are Kiwano's own, and deliberately carry no
declaration so the provenance of a file can be read off its header.


